	<http://sbols.org/v3#name> "BBa_I756033" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#description> "CD11a" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#description> "LFA1 is a human transmembrane receptor composed of CD18 and CD11a which bind to ICAM. In acute myocardial infarction ICAM is exposed on the cell surface and therefore is one of the ideal targets for repairing damaged heart tissue. \n\nTo transmit the signal, we used a split ubiquitin system (Cub and NubG) that will reconstitute mLexA-VP16 in vivo. MLexA-VP16 translocates to nucleus where is functions as the switch to upregulate expression of the rescue circuit, death circuit and cell adhesion circuit via the binding to the lexA operator minimal promoter." ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#author> "Jennifer Lei" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#source> "kpn1 (1-6bp)\n\nkozak (7-12bp)\n\nCD11a from pCDL1 (13-3525bp) Larson, RS et al. J Cell Bio, 108(2): 703-12, 1989\n\nstop stop (3526-3531bp)\n\nxba1 (3532-3537bp)" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#created> "2007-10-25T06:00:00.000Z" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#note> "none" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#status> "Planning" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#type> <https://identifiers.org/SBO:0000251> ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#hasSequence> <http://parts.igem.org/Part:BBa_I756033#sequence> .
<http://parts.igem.org/Part:BBa_I732917#feature2253356> a <http://sbols.org/v3#Component> ;
	<https://sbols.org/backport/2_3#sbol2OriginalURI> <http://parts.igem.org/Part:BBa_I732917#feature2253356> ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#displayId> "BBa_B0010" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#name> "BBa_B0010" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#type> <https://identifiers.org/SBO:0000251> .
<http://parts.igem.org/Part:BBa_I732924#feature2296554> a <http://sbols.org/v3#Component> ;
	<https://sbols.org/backport/2_3#sbol2OriginalURI> <http://parts.igem.org/Part:BBa_I732924#feature2296554> ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#displayId> "BBa_E1010" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#name> "BBa_E1010" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#type> <https://identifiers.org/SBO:0000251> .
<http://parts.igem.org/Part:BBa_I756035> a <http://sbols.org/v3#Component> ;
	<https://sbols.org/backport/2_3#sbol2OriginalURI> <http://parts.igem.org/Part:BBa_I756035> ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#displayId> "BBa_I756035" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#name> "BBa_I756035" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#description> "CD18-Cub-mlexA-linker-VP16" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#description> "CD18-Cub-mLexA-linker-VP16\n\nCD18 is the second half of the LFA1 signaling dimer which binds to ICAM. To induce an output from ligand mediated signaling, we used the split ubiquitin system. We designed LFA1 dimerisation to produce the same output as our other signaling receptors - mLexA-VP16." ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#author> "Jennifer Lei" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#source> "kpn1 (1-6bp)\n\nkozak (7-12bp)\n\nCD18 from Integrin beata2-mYFP, Kim, M et al. Science 2003, 5640:1720-5 (13-2319bp)\n\nBspQ1 linker (2320-2361bp) \n\nCub seembled from oligos (2362-2487bp)\n\nlinker (2488-2511bp)\n\nmLexA from PEG202 (2512-3201bp)\n\nlinker (3202-3234bp)\n\nVP16 from HSV1 helper virus (Salposky lab, Stanford) (3235-3372bp)\n\nStop Stop (3373-3378bp)\n\nXba1 (3379-3384bp)" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#created> "2007-10-25T06:00:00.000Z" ;
